Title: The Glass Catalogue
Credit: Original test fixture

INT. AURELIA AUCTION HOUSE - NIGHT

MIRA VOSS
The catalogue says the blue room was empty before the fire.

ELIAS RUNE
Your grandmother signed the inventory. Let the record stay buried.

Mira finds a silver moth seal beneath a false catalogue label. The seal proves that the missing paintings were moved after the fire.

INT. CITY ARCHIVE - MORNING

MIRA VOSS
If I expose the inventory, the board will erase my family from the house.

NORA VALE
Then make them defend the lie in public.

Mira compares the auction ledger with the fire report. Elias offers her the blue room studio if she withdraws the accusation.

INT. CHARITY AUCTION - NIGHT

Mira interrupts the sale and projects the altered inventory. The board turns on Elias. She rejects private ownership of the studio and converts it into a public workshop for young artists.
